  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This serves 4 as a snack and takes about 25 minutes. The thing to watch is the ripeness again: the plantain must be very ripe with mostly black skin. Yellow plantain gives you a starchy, bland result with none of the caramel sweetness that makes kelewele special."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut the plantain into rough cubes about 2cm square. Too small and they burn before the inside is cooked; too large and the spice does not reach the centre."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plantain",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "very ripe, black-skinned",
              "prepNote": "peeled and cut into 2cm cubes",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "ginger-fresh",
              "amount": 20,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "grated or finely minced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Spice mix"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chilli-red",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "finely chopped, or to taste",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Spice mix"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "allspice",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Spice mix"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 5,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "for shallow frying",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix together the ginger, chilli, allspice, and salt in a large bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the plantain cubes and toss to coat thoroughly in the spice mixture. Leave for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large frying pan over medium-high heat until shimmering."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the plantain cubes in a single layer. Do not crowd. Fry for 3-4 minutes until golden and caramelised on the underside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn and fry for another 2-3 minutes on the other side. Work in batches if needed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain on kitchen paper. Serve hot as a snack or alongside grilled fish and peanuts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Kelewele is not sweet and tastes savoury only",
              "cause": "Plantain not ripe enough",
              "fix": "Wait until the skin is at least 80 percent black before using"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Spice burns before the plantain is cooked through",
              "cause": "Oil too hot or cubes too small",
              "fix": "Use medium-high rather than high heat and cut cubes at least 2cm"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Plantain cubes are soft and greasy",
              "cause": "Oil not hot enough when they went in",
              "fix": "Test with one piece first - it should sizzle actively the moment it hits the oil"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kelewele is one of the most popular street foods in Ghana and is found at roadside stalls throughout Accra and across the country in the evenings. Vendors fry it in large woks and serve it in newspaper cones with roasted peanuts on the side. The combination of sweet plantain, hot chilli, and warming ginger is distinctly Ghanaian. It is also served as a side dish in Ghanaian restaurants worldwide."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
